        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0448" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg352"/>

                <head>No. 268.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 18, 1871</date>.
                        (Received December 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 472.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I herewith inclose copies and translations
                    of two important circulars that were issued by the minister of the treasury,
                    dated October <pb facs="0449" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/> 20 and October 30, for
                    the purpose of preventing frauds upon the treasury on the northern frontier, by
                    the importation of goods without the payment of the federal duties, and also to
                    enforce the payment of duties when foreign goods shall pass through the
                    territory occupied by the insurgents toward the interior. (A, B, C, and D.)</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d268-a1.xml" xpointer="d268-a1"/>
